>> title: Reheated Pizza with Hot Honey, Air Fryer
>> category: Pizzas
>> tags: pizza, leftovers, reheat, air fryer, basket, hot honey
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: reheated pizza, air fryer pizza slice, leftover pizza, day-old pizza, hot honey pizza
>> servings: 2
>> time: 12 min
>> slack: forgiving — the base is rigid at four minutes and still good at seven; it is the one dish here where being late costs nothing
>> washing-up: the basket, a small bowl
>> keeps: not at all — this is already the recipe for the day-old slice, and there is no day after that one

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. Cold slices from the fridge, one layer — a stacked slice steams the one below.
Cold from the fridge, one layer. The microwave steams the base; this dries it.

>> step: stir the chile honey in a small bowl
Stir @honey{2%Tbs}, @red chile flakes{1/2%tsp}, @dried oregano{1/4%tsp}, @extra-virgin olive oil{1%tsp} together in a #small bowl{}.

>> step: roast in the basket 180°C (350°F), 4–6 min, one layer
Roast @leftover pizza{4%slices}(cold, straight from the fridge) in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 180°C (350°F) for ~air fry{5%min}, one layer.

>> step: peel a corner up at four minutes — rigid base, cheese just loose
Peel @&(~1)pizza{} up by one corner.

>> step: drizzle straight out of the basket
Drizzle @&(~3)chile honey{} over @&(~1)hot slices{} with @flaky salt{1/4%tsp}.
